1
00:00:00,019 --> 00:00:01,531
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,533 --> 00:00:03,000
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:03,024 --> 00:00:05,024
(Episode 80)

4
00:00:14,526 --> 00:00:15,783
Leave Seoul.

5
00:00:15,818 --> 00:00:17,374
Go as far away as you can.

6
00:00:17,392 --> 00:00:19,254
- Go live somewhere far away.
- Really?

7
00:00:20,232 --> 00:00:21,360
But...

8
00:00:22,436 --> 00:00:24,348
I can't leave
until I've paid off all my debts.

9
00:00:26,229 --> 00:00:27,989
You said that back then too.

10
00:00:29,940 --> 00:00:31,261
How much do you owe?

11
00:00:32,132 --> 00:00:33,132
Two hundred thousand dollars.

12
00:00:33,429 --> 00:00:34,429
What?

13
00:00:34,992 --> 00:00:37,812
Pay that off, and I'll disappear. Forever.

14
00:00:38,526 --> 00:00:39,631
I promise.

15
00:00:39,891 --> 00:00:41,988
I'd love to pay you off
and get rid of you,

16
00:00:42,012 --> 00:00:45,270
- but I don't have that kind of money.
- Then find a way!

17
00:00:45,295 --> 00:00:46,615
You're a model, aren't you?

18
00:00:46,639 --> 00:00:48,215
Surely you have wealthy friends.

19
00:00:48,551 --> 00:00:51,101
If you go near my daughter,
you won't get another penny.

20
00:00:51,150 --> 00:00:52,467
Think carefully.

21
00:00:53,665 --> 00:00:57,245
If you want to get even a little money,
you'd better behave.

22
00:00:58,655 --> 00:00:59,655
Fine.

23
00:01:02,158 --> 00:01:04,405
Since you're here, clean up a bit.

24
00:01:06,122 --> 00:01:07,122
What?

25
00:01:07,412 --> 00:01:09,196
It's filthy in here.

26
00:01:09,298 --> 00:01:10,881
Mom used to do it for me,

27
00:01:11,791 --> 00:01:13,615
but that old hag went and died.

28
00:01:14,179 --> 00:01:17,512
- Did you kill her?
- Shut up and clean!

29
00:01:19,572 --> 00:01:21,760
- Want me to just blow everything up?
- Fine!

30
00:01:22,482 --> 00:01:23,598
I said fine.

31
00:01:32,905 --> 00:01:33,905
Get out.

32
00:01:33,982 --> 00:01:35,206
I won't do it while you're here.

33
00:01:37,037 --> 00:01:38,081
You're scared of me, aren't you?

34
00:02:24,165 --> 00:02:25,285
Hello.

35
00:02:25,678 --> 00:02:27,118
What brings you here?

36
00:02:27,369 --> 00:02:30,222
I came to see my mom.
Her birthday is tomorrow.

37
00:02:30,237 --> 00:02:31,743
She's not here right now.

38
00:02:32,180 --> 00:02:35,029
By the way, you're still studying
animation, right?

39
00:02:36,072 --> 00:02:38,363
- Want to take a look at this?
- Sure.

40
00:02:41,211 --> 00:02:43,814
This is an interview scene
for a documentary,

41
00:02:43,838 --> 00:02:46,387
but we don't have any footage
for the flashback.

42
00:02:46,772 --> 00:02:48,315
I'd like to add some drawings.

43
00:02:48,507 --> 00:02:51,502
- Do you think you can do it?
- I'll give it a try.

44
00:02:51,527 --> 00:02:53,804
Look at photos of the interviewee
as a child,

45
00:02:53,828 --> 00:02:56,903
then draw a few expressions
and poses in motion.

46
00:02:56,928 --> 00:02:59,009
That sounds fun.

47
00:02:59,172 --> 00:03:00,765
I've never done this kind of work before.

48
00:03:02,290 --> 00:03:03,340
The photos...

49
00:03:05,785 --> 00:03:07,412
I don't have them.

50
00:03:08,162 --> 00:03:09,420
They're at the office.

51
00:03:09,530 --> 00:03:11,777
Then I'll come by tomorrow.

52
00:03:11,801 --> 00:03:15,172
Okay. I'll pick out some examples too,

53
00:03:15,245 --> 00:03:16,843
- so you can study them.
- Okay.

54
00:03:20,391 --> 00:03:22,983
I thought you were angry with me.

55
00:03:23,466 --> 00:03:24,466
Why would I be?

56
00:03:24,772 --> 00:03:27,704
Because of Do Hee.
I told her to leave Korea.

57
00:03:29,198 --> 00:03:30,560
Let's drop that subject.

58
00:03:50,124 --> 00:03:51,124
Mom.

59
00:03:52,908 --> 00:03:54,604
Mom, what happened to you?

60
00:03:55,855 --> 00:03:58,102
Why are you here?

61
00:03:58,971 --> 00:04:00,520
I need to talk to you about something.

62
00:04:00,545 --> 00:04:01,545
What?

63
00:04:02,333 --> 00:04:03,615
Wait a minute.

64
00:04:03,757 --> 00:04:05,247
I'll go wash up first.

65
00:04:14,938 --> 00:04:17,267
Your mother-in-law's birthday
is tomorrow too?

66
00:04:17,359 --> 00:04:18,511
The same day as mine?

67
00:04:19,324 --> 00:04:20,888
Just my luck.

68
00:04:21,836 --> 00:04:24,345
Don't be like that. She's family now.

69
00:04:25,245 --> 00:04:26,385
Anyway,

70
00:04:26,615 --> 00:04:29,625
I figured I'd have to spend
the evening with my in-laws,

71
00:04:29,649 --> 00:04:32,145
so I thought we'd have lunch with Ji Hu.

72
00:04:32,438 --> 00:04:34,690
I booked the restaurant
Dad used to take us to.

73
00:04:34,813 --> 00:04:37,028
Forget it. It'll just make me sadder.

74
00:04:37,500 --> 00:04:38,846
Then should we go somewhere else?

75
00:04:39,114 --> 00:04:40,398
I said forget it.

76
00:04:41,044 --> 00:04:44,028
Don't worry about me.
Focus on your in-laws.

77
00:04:44,339 --> 00:04:45,880
Go. I'm tired.

78
00:04:47,042 --> 00:04:49,123
What have you been doing to get so tired?

79
00:04:49,272 --> 00:04:50,681
Is it menopause?

80
00:04:51,152 --> 00:04:52,538
I hear red ginseng helps with that.

81
00:04:52,584 --> 00:04:53,756
What's gotten into you?

82
00:04:54,238 --> 00:04:55,734
Getting married made you grow up?

83
00:04:56,763 --> 00:04:59,196
I drove you crazy when I was a teenager.

84
00:04:59,220 --> 00:05:01,776
You do know that, right?

85
00:05:04,047 --> 00:05:07,232
Now that you have a husband,
do you feel sorry for your widowed mom?

86
00:05:08,445 --> 00:05:11,353
Anyway, lunch tomorrow. Got it?

87
00:05:11,378 --> 00:05:13,367
You're such a nuisance.

88
00:05:13,692 --> 00:05:17,693
Don't worry about me.
Focus on your mother-in-law's birthday.

89
00:05:17,717 --> 00:05:19,006
It's your first one since getting married.

90
00:05:19,030 --> 00:05:20,410
How can I do that?

91
00:05:20,483 --> 00:05:22,097
I have to take care of both of you.

92
00:05:22,558 --> 00:05:25,469
Since when have you made
such a fuss over my birthday?

93
00:05:25,494 --> 00:05:26,810
Don't you remember?

94
00:05:26,812 --> 00:05:29,974
On your dad's birthday, you stormed out,
saying you'd never come back.

95
00:05:30,645 --> 00:05:32,242
Do you know how much I regret that?

96
00:05:32,266 --> 00:05:33,882
Enough.

97
00:05:33,972 --> 00:05:35,714
I get how you feel. Let's stop.

98
00:05:37,344 --> 00:05:38,705
This is so unfair.

99
00:05:39,232 --> 00:05:42,127
Would I feel right only celebrating
my mother-in-law's birthday?

100
00:05:42,444 --> 00:05:44,282
Am I the only one? What about Ji Hu?

101
00:05:44,772 --> 00:05:48,153
It's his first time celebrating
his mother-in-law's birthday.

102
00:05:48,523 --> 00:05:50,820
- Na Ji Ni...
- When I refused, you involved Jung A...

103
00:05:50,845 --> 00:05:52,114
and kept pressuring me.

104
00:05:53,873 --> 00:05:55,004
Do whatever you want.

105
00:05:55,632 --> 00:05:58,184
Ji Ni!

106
00:06:02,685 --> 00:06:03,685
That girl...

107
00:06:05,455 --> 00:06:06,743
My whole body aches.

108
00:06:16,207 --> 00:06:17,718
(Don't pick up)

109
00:06:24,658 --> 00:06:26,263
I told you not to call me.

110
00:06:26,305 --> 00:06:28,449
The place is spotless.

111
00:06:28,988 --> 00:06:30,857
You did a good job, ma'am.

112
00:06:30,881 --> 00:06:32,014
"Ma'am?"

113
00:06:32,071 --> 00:06:33,703
Do I look like your maid?

114
00:06:34,332 --> 00:06:35,769
I cleaned up as you asked,

115
00:06:35,770 --> 00:06:38,086
and I even handed you money.
So show me some respect.

116
00:06:38,111 --> 00:06:39,678
Stop calling me whenever you feel like it.

117
00:06:39,702 --> 00:06:40,968
Okay, I get it.

118
00:06:40,993 --> 00:06:43,519
I was genuinely touched.
I just called to thank you.

119
00:06:43,544 --> 00:06:44,544
Enough.

120
00:06:44,569 --> 00:06:47,244
Don't contact me again
until the payment date.

121
00:06:47,725 --> 00:06:51,666
And if I catch you hanging around
my daughter again,

122
00:06:52,136 --> 00:06:54,266
I'll blow everything wide open,
money or no money.

123
00:06:54,290 --> 00:06:56,990
And we'll both go straight to the abyss.
Got it?

124
00:06:57,605 --> 00:06:59,632
You've got quite a temper.

125
00:06:59,657 --> 00:07:02,677
Try me if you want to find out
whether I'm serious.

126
00:07:03,045 --> 00:07:05,383
You think I'm living like this
because I have no temper?

127
00:07:12,212 --> 00:07:13,212
Fine.

128
00:07:14,554 --> 00:07:17,282
I'll pay the price.

129
00:07:18,345 --> 00:07:22,209
I'll pay for what I did to Yeong Ju.

130
00:07:43,932 --> 00:07:44,932
What are you doing?

131
00:07:46,292 --> 00:07:47,380
Seung Woo...

132
00:07:48,342 --> 00:07:49,743
Director...

133
00:07:50,247 --> 00:07:53,840
asked me to draw some animation
for a documentary, so I'm practicing.

134
00:07:53,864 --> 00:07:55,428
Really? Seung Woo?

135
00:07:55,771 --> 00:07:56,771
That's great.

136
00:07:57,958 --> 00:07:59,423
But you still call him Director?

137
00:07:59,912 --> 00:08:01,390
Can't you call him Seung Woo?

138
00:08:03,382 --> 00:08:04,470
It just won't come out.

139
00:08:05,205 --> 00:08:07,537
I guess that kind of relationship
is harder than it seems.

140
00:08:08,265 --> 00:08:10,958
I feel like I have to watch
every little thing I say.

141
00:08:11,846 --> 00:08:15,066
At first, I couldn't even look him
in the eye. I was so intimidated.

142
00:08:16,538 --> 00:08:19,728
Still, we had
a comfortable conversation today.

143
00:08:20,244 --> 00:08:22,907
But the moment I mentioned Do Hee,
he turned cold.

144
00:08:22,984 --> 00:08:23,984
Do Hee?

145
00:08:25,131 --> 00:08:26,959
That name feels like a lifetime ago.

146
00:08:27,632 --> 00:08:29,038
So much has happened since then.

147
00:08:29,167 --> 00:08:30,167
It really has.

148
00:08:30,225 --> 00:08:32,311
It feels like ages ago to me too.

149
00:08:35,836 --> 00:08:38,488
Does your mom have time tomorrow?

150
00:08:38,704 --> 00:08:40,907
She says it's a hassle. Maybe she's busy.

151
00:08:41,366 --> 00:08:43,578
Don't worry about it.
My mom's always like that.

152
00:08:43,604 --> 00:08:46,237
Still, it's her first birthday
since your dad passed away.

153
00:08:46,699 --> 00:08:48,101
You said she used to celebrate in style.

154
00:08:48,345 --> 00:08:50,645
Forget it. Let's just focus on
your mom's birthday.

155
00:08:54,413 --> 00:08:56,616
No. I'll go.

156
00:09:04,724 --> 00:09:06,140
- Welcome home.
- Yeah.

157
00:09:12,745 --> 00:09:14,945
You two look like newlyweds.

158
00:09:15,645 --> 00:09:17,669
- Welcome back, Father.
- Thanks.

159
00:09:17,694 --> 00:09:19,620
- Have you eaten?
- Yes, I have.

160
00:09:20,485 --> 00:09:21,485
My dear daughter-in-law!

161
00:09:22,142 --> 00:09:24,467
- How's it going? Settling in okay?
- Yes, Father.

162
00:09:24,951 --> 00:09:27,084
- You must be tired.
- No, I'm fine.

163
00:09:27,612 --> 00:09:29,239
Ji Hu, come see me for a minute.

164
00:09:29,389 --> 00:09:30,389
Yes, Dad.

165
00:09:37,198 --> 00:09:38,843
- What are you doing?
- Sorry?

166
00:09:38,936 --> 00:09:40,328
Shouldn't you be doing your work?

167
00:09:50,719 --> 00:09:54,324
At the exhibition, I saw publishers
trying all sorts of interesting things.

168
00:09:54,592 --> 00:09:56,622
They're collaborating
with webtoon studios...

169
00:09:56,726 --> 00:09:58,439
to create visual content.

170
00:09:58,483 --> 00:10:00,091
I thought we could do the same...

171
00:10:00,104 --> 00:10:02,793
and make visually striking books that
could be adapted for the screen.

172
00:10:03,118 --> 00:10:04,473
Why don't you come up with a proposal?

173
00:10:04,804 --> 00:10:05,804
Sure. I will.

174
00:10:06,492 --> 00:10:08,938
Is Ji Ni not planning to return
to publishing?

175
00:10:08,963 --> 00:10:11,326
Animation was what she originally
wanted to do.

176
00:10:11,806 --> 00:10:13,419
She's preparing to create her own work.

177
00:10:13,443 --> 00:10:14,731
Is that so?

178
00:10:15,229 --> 00:10:18,255
Tomorrow is your mom's birthday.
Invite your mother-in-law too.

179
00:10:18,352 --> 00:10:20,255
You'll get closer
if you see each other often.

180
00:10:20,452 --> 00:10:22,298
She's alone without her husband.

181
00:10:22,392 --> 00:10:23,587
Actually,

182
00:10:23,775 --> 00:10:25,356
it's my mother-in-law's birthday
tomorrow too.

183
00:10:25,380 --> 00:10:27,491
Really? That's perfect.

184
00:10:27,605 --> 00:10:29,825
Then call and invite her
to celebrate together.

185
00:10:30,173 --> 00:10:33,020
But it seems she told Ji Ni
to focus on my mom's birthday.

186
00:10:33,045 --> 00:10:35,551
That's not right. How could we do that?

187
00:10:35,576 --> 00:10:37,647
I think Ji Ni feels caught in the middle.

188
00:10:37,905 --> 00:10:39,347
And I'm in an awkward position too.

189
00:10:40,031 --> 00:10:41,031
What should I do?

190
00:10:43,792 --> 00:10:46,173
- Well, I'll give her a call.
- You will, Dad?

191
00:10:46,198 --> 00:10:48,671
They say a daughter-in-law's best ally is
her father-in-law.

192
00:10:50,241 --> 00:10:51,372
Thank you so much, Dad.

193
00:10:51,397 --> 00:10:53,960
If you're grateful, treat your mom well.

194
00:10:54,325 --> 00:10:55,600
That's all I ask.

195
00:10:55,977 --> 00:10:56,977
Yes.

196
00:11:19,947 --> 00:11:22,632
You should've said you wanted
seaweed soup.

197
00:11:23,305 --> 00:11:25,369
It's not for me.

198
00:11:27,006 --> 00:11:29,718
What? For me?

199
00:11:30,734 --> 00:11:32,880
For my birthday?

200
00:11:32,905 --> 00:11:34,475
I heard yesterday.

201
00:11:34,625 --> 00:11:37,204
I can't make it myself.
Seung Hyun can, though.

202
00:11:38,167 --> 00:11:41,857
They say Seung Hyun is reserved and
you're the affectionate one. It's true.

203
00:11:42,312 --> 00:11:44,095
I bet you wish Ji Ni were here,

204
00:11:44,236 --> 00:11:46,816
but anyway...

205
00:11:48,271 --> 00:11:50,478
I have no idea what you're trying to say.

206
00:11:50,931 --> 00:11:52,331
Anyway, thank you.

207
00:11:52,798 --> 00:11:55,414
Ji Ni's busy today.
It's her mother-in-law's birthday.

208
00:11:55,439 --> 00:11:57,576
I'll just have a little party on my own.

209
00:11:58,084 --> 00:12:01,167
Her mother-in-law didn't seem
very pleasant.

210
00:12:01,191 --> 00:12:02,320
Right?

211
00:12:02,552 --> 00:12:05,750
Women who marry well
never seem to grow up.

212
00:12:06,438 --> 00:12:09,917
Ji Ni asked me to have lunch with her,
but I was so annoyed.

213
00:12:10,168 --> 00:12:12,088
I told her to focus on her in-laws.

214
00:12:12,572 --> 00:12:13,905
At least enjoy this.

215
00:12:14,045 --> 00:12:15,886
And spare me the sweet talk.

216
00:12:17,669 --> 00:12:18,669
Thank you.

217
00:12:28,551 --> 00:12:31,806
Why are you doing this now?
What am I supposed to do?

218
00:12:36,672 --> 00:12:38,030
What's that?

219
00:12:38,907 --> 00:12:39,907
This?

220
00:12:40,583 --> 00:12:41,753
It's a credit ledger.

221
00:12:41,809 --> 00:12:42,809
A credit ledger?

222
00:12:47,494 --> 00:12:49,583
All of this is unpaid?

223
00:12:50,292 --> 00:12:51,611
Why aren't you collecting payment?

224
00:12:51,636 --> 00:12:54,535
The patients are all close to Doctor Lim.

225
00:12:54,717 --> 00:12:56,540
So he sends them medicine for free...

226
00:12:56,565 --> 00:12:58,634
and lets them pay whenever they can.

227
00:12:58,831 --> 00:13:01,847
Honestly, I don't think he even intends
to collect the money.

228
00:13:02,184 --> 00:13:03,599
Still, we have to keep records.

229
00:13:03,865 --> 00:13:05,158
You never know what might happen.

230
00:13:06,321 --> 00:13:07,321
Unbelievable.

231
00:13:07,412 --> 00:13:10,178
At least he doesn't have rent to pay,

232
00:13:10,601 --> 00:13:12,428
but he still has loans to pay off.

233
00:13:13,578 --> 00:13:16,159
Doctor Lim is just too kind.

234
00:13:17,377 --> 00:13:18,835
He has loans?

235
00:13:27,174 --> 00:13:29,935
Sa Bin, are you Albert Schweitzer?

236
00:13:30,416 --> 00:13:33,047
- What?
- Why aren't you charging your patients?

237
00:13:33,278 --> 00:13:35,147
Why are you giving away
so many free treatments?

238
00:13:35,172 --> 00:13:37,352
How did you...

239
00:13:37,891 --> 00:13:40,778
Look how much is still unpaid
in this credit ledger.

240
00:13:40,939 --> 00:13:43,202
That's not kindness. It's stupidity.

241
00:13:43,227 --> 00:13:44,227
Yeong Ju,

242
00:13:44,729 --> 00:13:46,909
the reason I became
a Korean Medicine Doctor...

243
00:13:48,792 --> 00:13:51,178
But why should I have to
explain myself to you?

244
00:13:51,384 --> 00:13:53,397
Have I ever let you go hungry?

245
00:13:53,422 --> 00:13:55,818
Have I ever fallen behind
on household expenses?

246
00:13:56,365 --> 00:13:59,983
It's my money. If I choose not
to collect it, what's the problem?

247
00:14:01,725 --> 00:14:04,091
Helping people in need is a good thing.

248
00:14:04,156 --> 00:14:06,690
But you still need
to have some basic principles.

249
00:14:07,047 --> 00:14:10,176
Sa Bin, I heard you have loans to pay off.
Why are you spending money so carelessly?

250
00:14:10,201 --> 00:14:13,989
It's not that I don't charge them.
I let them buy on credit.

251
00:14:14,665 --> 00:14:15,665
And...

252
00:14:15,895 --> 00:14:19,489
why are you so concerned about
my finances?

253
00:14:19,562 --> 00:14:20,562
Your money?

254
00:14:21,119 --> 00:14:22,325
Your finances?

255
00:14:23,012 --> 00:14:26,149
Do you realize you're not in a position
to say that to me?

256
00:14:27,094 --> 00:14:30,014
Even if we're married,
I'd rather you not interfere like this.

257
00:14:31,419 --> 00:14:32,624
Okay.

258
00:14:32,791 --> 00:14:35,357
Then I won't say another word.

259
00:14:36,219 --> 00:14:37,748
I was just meddling.

260
00:14:42,327 --> 00:14:45,414
That's not it. The tabs...

261
00:14:45,562 --> 00:14:49,002
I want to stop allowing them,
but I just can't seem to.

262
00:14:49,555 --> 00:14:50,977
I'll try from now on.

263
00:14:51,552 --> 00:14:52,634
Then,

264
00:14:52,989 --> 00:14:54,812
can I help you from now on?

265
00:14:55,152 --> 00:14:56,915
Even if it means playing the bad guy,

266
00:14:56,939 --> 00:15:00,348
if you want me to get rid of
that tab for good, I'll do it.

267
00:15:00,372 --> 00:15:02,653
Otherwise, you can keep living like this.

268
00:15:03,105 --> 00:15:04,899
Just decide and let me know.

269
00:15:05,052 --> 00:15:07,065
I'll do whatever you want.

270
00:15:27,726 --> 00:15:28,726
This is him.

271
00:15:29,562 --> 00:15:31,229
My nephew remembered him.

272
00:15:31,240 --> 00:15:33,336
He had a simple name. Lee Cheol.

273
00:15:33,490 --> 00:15:34,727
Lee Cheol.

274
00:15:36,610 --> 00:15:39,115
Would it be okay if I returned this later?

275
00:15:39,176 --> 00:15:41,044
- Sure.
- Thank you.

276
00:15:43,600 --> 00:15:45,062
Almost forgot!

277
00:15:47,410 --> 00:15:48,573
Take care.

278
00:15:55,191 --> 00:15:58,729
Seung Hyun, get me an iced Americano.

279
00:15:58,800 --> 00:16:00,071
I'm boiling mad.

280
00:16:00,989 --> 00:16:02,644
Here. I haven't touched it.

281
00:16:08,930 --> 00:16:09,930
Charge me.

282
00:16:10,629 --> 00:16:13,218
- It's fine.
- You too? No charge?

283
00:16:14,185 --> 00:16:15,623
Are you all rich or something?

284
00:16:15,941 --> 00:16:17,625
You're running a business. Charge me.

285
00:16:17,627 --> 00:16:18,993
Mom, not again...

286
00:16:20,362 --> 00:16:21,769
Fine. I'll let you pay.

287
00:16:28,123 --> 00:16:29,473
What's this?

288
00:16:30,783 --> 00:16:33,559
- Seo Chon Middle School? Is this yours?
- No.

289
00:16:38,352 --> 00:16:41,094
They say this is him.
The Pumseonggak owner's son.

290
00:16:41,814 --> 00:16:42,888
What?

291
00:16:43,626 --> 00:16:47,006
Is this guy the motorcycle rider?

292
00:16:47,112 --> 00:16:49,524
We're not sure yet. We need to check.

293
00:16:49,595 --> 00:16:51,006
How can we check?

294
00:16:51,070 --> 00:16:52,500
With this childhood photo?

295
00:16:53,052 --> 00:16:55,667
They say if you run an old photo
through an AI program,

296
00:16:55,717 --> 00:16:59,187
it can predict what the person
looks like now.

297
00:17:00,197 --> 00:17:01,614
Good thinking.

298
00:17:02,955 --> 00:17:06,993
It was a local accident, so he probably
went to a nearby middle school.

299
00:17:15,294 --> 00:17:18,107
You're eligible to borrow
up to 50,000 dollars.

300
00:17:18,192 --> 00:17:20,812
The annual interest rate is 16.5 percent.

301
00:17:20,880 --> 00:17:22,088
Would you like to proceed?

302
00:17:24,863 --> 00:17:28,471
How on earth does this bastard owe
200,000 dollars?

303
00:17:32,770 --> 00:17:34,485
Should I just kill him?

304
00:17:42,973 --> 00:17:44,362
(Lim Joong Bin)

305
00:17:48,652 --> 00:17:50,040
Yes, sir.

306
00:17:54,286 --> 00:17:56,832
Why did you suddenly ask to see me?

307
00:17:59,082 --> 00:18:00,771
It's your birthday today.

308
00:18:01,393 --> 00:18:02,812
Yes, what a coincidence!

309
00:18:02,884 --> 00:18:05,980
It happens to be the same day
as your wife's birthday.

310
00:18:06,372 --> 00:18:09,628
I know you're busy, but I'd
still like us to have dinner tonight.

311
00:18:10,330 --> 00:18:13,773
I heard you turned me down,
so I wanted to ask you in person.

312
00:18:14,602 --> 00:18:15,602
Ma'am,

313
00:18:16,412 --> 00:18:17,658
I know this may be uncomfortable...

314
00:18:17,726 --> 00:18:19,462
No, really. It's fine.

315
00:18:19,722 --> 00:18:22,863
You could've just called
if that's all you wanted.

316
00:18:23,461 --> 00:18:24,689
I understand.

317
00:18:25,680 --> 00:18:27,701
But please come. For Ji Ni's sake.

318
00:18:28,032 --> 00:18:29,446
And for Ji Hu too.

319
00:18:29,696 --> 00:18:33,040
Isn't it a parent's job
to put their children's minds at ease?

320
00:18:33,818 --> 00:18:35,545
I understand what you're saying,

321
00:18:35,769 --> 00:18:38,933
but I've been having a hard time lately.
I just don't have the energy.

322
00:18:39,672 --> 00:18:42,252
Is something wrong?

323
00:18:42,612 --> 00:18:44,823
You seemed so uneasy at the wedding too.

324
00:18:45,190 --> 00:18:46,989
I've been worried about you.

325
00:18:47,873 --> 00:18:50,421
Please tell me if there's anything
I can do.

326
00:18:52,002 --> 00:18:55,302
- Well, Joong Bin.
- What?

327
00:18:57,886 --> 00:18:59,145
Yes, ma'am.

328
00:19:01,132 --> 00:19:02,871
No, Se Ri.

329
00:19:03,974 --> 00:19:07,678
I don't think I can talk to you
if I keep thinking of us as in-laws.

330
00:19:07,789 --> 00:19:10,735
But since we were friends once,

331
00:19:11,098 --> 00:19:14,199
I know I have no right to ask,
but I need your advice.

332
00:19:14,400 --> 00:19:15,595
Of course.

333
00:19:15,654 --> 00:19:19,064
If you're doing well,
Ji Ni will be at ease too.

334
00:19:20,952 --> 00:19:22,312
I'm trying...

335
00:19:23,069 --> 00:19:25,647
to start a small business,

336
00:19:25,886 --> 00:19:27,604
but I'm a little short on funds.

337
00:19:27,663 --> 00:19:29,107
- A business?
- Yes.

338
00:19:29,170 --> 00:19:32,114
A friend and I
were setting up a boutique...

339
00:19:32,352 --> 00:19:34,304
Were you scammed?

340
00:19:34,682 --> 00:19:36,692
I'm ashamed to say it, but yes.

341
00:19:37,270 --> 00:19:41,162
My friend took all the money
and disappeared.

342
00:19:41,472 --> 00:19:42,852
Did you trust your friend too much?

343
00:19:43,604 --> 00:19:47,551
It's not just my friend. There's also
the man she borrowed money from.

344
00:19:48,910 --> 00:19:50,697
I see what happened.

345
00:19:51,747 --> 00:19:53,596
You got mixed up with a dangerous man.

346
00:19:54,552 --> 00:19:56,104
How much do you owe?

347
00:19:58,173 --> 00:20:00,084
Two hundred thousand dollars.

348
00:20:01,407 --> 00:20:02,762
When do you need it by?

349
00:20:03,146 --> 00:20:04,698
I'll see what I can do.

350
00:20:05,747 --> 00:20:10,142
But dealing with a man like that
yourself might be difficult.

351
00:20:10,770 --> 00:20:12,160
Why not put him in touch with me?

352
00:20:12,576 --> 00:20:15,000
No, I'll handle it myself.

353
00:20:15,793 --> 00:20:17,453
I just need you to lend me the money.

354
00:20:18,176 --> 00:20:21,720
I'm actually getting quite a bit of work
as a model these days.

355
00:20:22,411 --> 00:20:25,722
I'm getting plenty of offers
from both older and younger people.

356
00:20:26,170 --> 00:20:29,463
- I promise I'll pay you back.
- Okay.

357
00:20:30,012 --> 00:20:32,771
Then I'll see you tonight...

358
00:20:32,833 --> 00:20:34,104
for the kids' sake.

359
00:20:35,233 --> 00:20:39,709
Okay. Please keep it a secret from Ji Ni.

360
00:20:40,011 --> 00:20:41,486
Of course.

361
00:20:52,012 --> 00:20:53,012
Yes?

362
00:20:58,058 --> 00:20:59,158
It's been a while.

363
00:21:00,906 --> 00:21:02,139
I heard you needed a writer.

364
00:21:08,532 --> 00:21:09,532
What?

365
00:21:09,711 --> 00:21:11,910
That's all you have to say
after all this time?

366
00:21:13,210 --> 00:21:14,732
I'm here for an interview.

367
00:21:14,952 --> 00:21:17,155
- I heard you needed a narration writer.
- Get out.

368
00:21:17,524 --> 00:21:20,079
- I'm not accepting your application.
- Can't you just judge me by my skills?

369
00:21:20,472 --> 00:21:21,734
You know how good I am.

370
00:21:22,332 --> 00:21:23,422
Or...

371
00:21:24,307 --> 00:21:25,528
are you still mad at me?

372
00:21:26,328 --> 00:21:28,892
I don't need a reason.
You're not getting the job.

373
00:21:29,381 --> 00:21:30,381
Get out.

374
00:21:32,416 --> 00:21:33,666
I'm here.

375
00:21:40,301 --> 00:21:41,812
Hold on.

376
00:21:55,574 --> 00:21:56,856
Don't come back!

377
00:21:57,188 --> 00:21:58,397
I got divorced.

378
00:21:59,258 --> 00:22:01,635
- Did you hear me?
- What does that have to do with me?

379
00:22:02,590 --> 00:22:04,091
I did it for you.

380
00:22:04,812 --> 00:22:06,534
I wanted to date you properly.

381
00:22:07,263 --> 00:22:08,396
What about your daughter?

382
00:22:08,938 --> 00:22:10,109
But you're a mom.

383
00:22:10,240 --> 00:22:13,214
You're still the same person you were.

384
00:22:13,872 --> 00:22:15,991
You think hearing your family fell apart
because of me...

385
00:22:16,353 --> 00:22:18,884
would make me say, "Good for you?"

386
00:22:18,930 --> 00:22:20,694
I'm living with my daughter.

387
00:22:21,532 --> 00:22:23,093
That's why I need more money.

388
00:22:23,730 --> 00:22:24,846
Please help me.

389
00:22:25,351 --> 00:22:26,539
Not here.

390
00:22:27,557 --> 00:22:28,793
You're talented.

391
00:22:28,932 --> 00:22:30,349
I'm sure you can find work elsewhere.

392
00:22:31,040 --> 00:22:32,138
Just go.

393
00:22:33,869 --> 00:22:35,050
Seung Woo.

394
00:22:37,570 --> 00:22:39,584
It was nice seeing you again.

395
00:22:41,830 --> 00:22:44,530
Good to see you doing well.

396
00:23:02,459 --> 00:23:03,631
Pretend you didn't see her.

397
00:23:05,230 --> 00:23:06,496
What happened?

398
00:23:07,572 --> 00:23:08,887
Just pretend you didn't see her.

399
00:23:10,517 --> 00:23:11,517
USB.

400
00:23:13,494 --> 00:23:14,494
Okay.

401
00:23:19,090 --> 00:23:20,090
What are you doing?

402
00:23:20,480 --> 00:23:21,969
It's your mother-in-law's birthday today.

403
00:23:22,270 --> 00:23:24,236
Isn't this the busiest day
for a daughter-in-law?

404
00:23:26,336 --> 00:23:30,271
I heard you made seaweed soup
for my mom this morning.

405
00:23:31,183 --> 00:23:32,277
Thank you.

406
00:23:33,250 --> 00:23:35,146
Go on. Don't worry.

407
00:23:36,665 --> 00:23:37,665
Okay.

408
00:23:48,480 --> 00:23:51,494
(Resume, Han Jeong Won)

409
00:24:03,205 --> 00:24:04,416
Look at this.

410
00:24:07,061 --> 00:24:09,503
This is hilarious!

411
00:24:09,941 --> 00:24:12,623
- Is this what's popular these days?
- Yes, it's like this.

412
00:24:13,150 --> 00:24:14,479
It's hilarious, right?

413
00:24:16,454 --> 00:24:17,511
Ji Ni.

414
00:24:18,290 --> 00:24:21,023
- I'm home, Mother.
- Yeah.

415
00:24:21,107 --> 00:24:22,416
What brings you here?

416
00:24:23,427 --> 00:24:25,301
I heard it was her birthday.

417
00:24:25,390 --> 00:24:27,250
After all, she's done so much for me.

418
00:24:28,330 --> 00:24:30,320
Ma'am, I've stayed too long.

419
00:24:30,370 --> 00:24:32,062
I was just going to drop off your gift.

420
00:24:32,614 --> 00:24:35,654
No, stay a little longer.
Have dinner before you go.

421
00:24:35,830 --> 00:24:38,545
You've made me laugh so much today.

422
00:24:41,536 --> 00:24:45,035
Neither Ji Hu nor this one is very warm,

423
00:24:45,130 --> 00:24:47,298
but you're always so witty!

424
00:24:47,890 --> 00:24:49,675
Thank you for being so nice to me.

425
00:24:49,743 --> 00:24:51,979
My mom scolds me for not acting my age.

426
00:24:52,492 --> 00:24:54,564
You're just adorable.

427
00:24:55,212 --> 00:24:58,354
Having a child who's so affectionate
is such a blessing.

428
00:24:59,916 --> 00:25:01,382
That's funny.

429
00:25:01,932 --> 00:25:05,372
What are you doing? Your friend's here.
Go get us something.

430
00:25:06,471 --> 00:25:07,688
Okay.

431
00:25:14,012 --> 00:25:15,271
Were you here?

432
00:25:20,202 --> 00:25:22,092
Are you making all the food yourself?

433
00:25:22,144 --> 00:25:23,724
It's an annual tradition. No big deal.

434
00:25:24,955 --> 00:25:27,601
- Here, take this out.
- Okay.

435
00:25:28,692 --> 00:25:31,269
- I'll help out too.
- Then thanks!

436
00:25:40,188 --> 00:25:42,985
Don't you even check the temperature?

437
00:25:43,932 --> 00:25:45,056
Seriously!

438
00:25:45,128 --> 00:25:47,338
Jung A, don't drink that. It's still hot.

439
00:25:47,928 --> 00:25:50,218
- Okay.
- I'll get you some ice.

440
00:25:50,296 --> 00:25:51,994
Forget it.

441
00:25:52,648 --> 00:25:55,482
Jung A, tell me that joke again.

442
00:25:56,193 --> 00:25:57,212
Sure.

443
00:25:59,006 --> 00:26:02,652
- Yeah, that one! That's hilarious.
- Right?

444
00:26:04,871 --> 00:26:06,127
You're here.

445
00:26:09,418 --> 00:26:12,604
- Hello.
- Jung A, you came too?

446
00:26:12,640 --> 00:26:15,396
- Good! It's nice to see you.
- Well, here I am.

447
00:26:15,827 --> 00:26:17,387
- Ji Hu.
- Yeah.

448
00:26:18,103 --> 00:26:20,309
You invited Jung A too? Good thinking.

449
00:26:21,385 --> 00:26:22,385
Mom.

450
00:26:22,809 --> 00:26:24,806
Yeah, I brought her along.

451
00:26:25,498 --> 00:26:27,752
Happy birthday.

452
00:26:28,404 --> 00:26:29,760
You shouldn't have!

453
00:26:29,861 --> 00:26:31,086
Thank you.

454
00:26:31,088 --> 00:26:35,570
Both mothers-in-law share the same
birthday. What a special connection!

455
00:26:36,387 --> 00:26:38,825
Yeah. I've never seen that before.

456
00:26:39,246 --> 00:26:41,959
- Mother, I'll put these in a vase.
- Okay.

457
00:26:43,427 --> 00:26:45,246
Ji Ni, give me the vase.

458
00:26:45,310 --> 00:26:47,410
- I'll arrange the flowers.
- Okay.

459
00:26:49,760 --> 00:26:51,596
The flowers are so pretty!

460
00:26:51,598 --> 00:26:54,888
As always, she's so elegant.

461
00:26:57,309 --> 00:26:59,139
Mom, everything's ready.

462
00:27:01,392 --> 00:27:04,002
You should smile more, too.

463
00:27:04,096 --> 00:27:05,191
Look at Jung A.

464
00:27:05,271 --> 00:27:08,714
She's so cheerful and sweet,
while you look so grumpy.

465
00:27:09,190 --> 00:27:11,944
I've told you to be nicer to your elders.

466
00:27:13,141 --> 00:27:14,896
How can I smile when I don't feel like it?

467
00:27:14,960 --> 00:27:16,740
Do you think I'm smiling
because I'm amused?

468
00:27:16,812 --> 00:27:19,521
I'm smiling to make them feel comfortable.

469
00:27:19,600 --> 00:27:20,885
It's frustrating for me too.

470
00:27:21,070 --> 00:27:23,983
How can I smile when she says
even my smile looks sad?

471
00:27:24,682 --> 00:27:27,230
Did Sun Kyung say that?

472
00:27:28,480 --> 00:27:30,012
No.

473
00:27:30,412 --> 00:27:32,185
That's not exactly what I meant.

474
00:27:33,338 --> 00:27:34,640
Anyway, hurry downstairs.

475
00:27:41,654 --> 00:27:46,454
What do you call a chicken
in really tight clothes?

476
00:27:46,572 --> 00:27:48,537
"A chicken in tight clothes?" What's that?

477
00:27:49,671 --> 00:27:51,370
- Cock-a-doodle-tight!
- My goodness!

478
00:27:52,783 --> 00:27:55,240
That's hilarious!

479
00:27:55,738 --> 00:27:56,922
Jung A, tell us another one.

480
00:27:56,997 --> 00:27:59,120
He loves these silly jokes.

481
00:27:59,313 --> 00:28:01,221
I should write these down
so I can remember them.

482
00:28:12,218 --> 00:28:14,610
"Cock-a-doodle-tight!" My goodness!

483
00:28:15,612 --> 00:28:17,896
I've got another one.
What's a burger's favorite color?

484
00:28:18,345 --> 00:28:19,479
"A burger?"

485
00:28:19,553 --> 00:28:20,950
Burgundy!

486
00:28:21,850 --> 00:28:24,989
She's so clever! My goodness!

487
00:28:25,124 --> 00:28:26,366
Honey.

488
00:28:47,130 --> 00:28:50,261
(Family Register)

489
00:28:50,328 --> 00:28:52,711
I need Jung A around.
I love spending time with her.

490
00:28:52,762 --> 00:28:54,273
I'll send 200,000 dollars tomorrow.

491
00:28:54,383 --> 00:28:56,273
- Really?
- Don't help her.

492
00:28:56,315 --> 00:28:57,810
She's not worth it.

493
00:28:57,869 --> 00:29:01,090
- Was this on your camera?
- Then why did you say you didn't see it?

494
00:29:01,149 --> 00:29:02,416
Were you always like this?

495
00:29:02,472 --> 00:29:04,212
I wish you were my daughter-in-law.

496
00:29:04,265 --> 00:29:07,398
A daughter-in-law isn't my daughter.
Why can't you just replace her?

497
00:29:09,110 --> 00:29:11,110
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
